    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d162">

                <pb facs="0443" n="408" xml:id="pg408"/>

                <head>162. Note From President Carter to Multiple Recipients<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d162-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1978-03-27">March 27, 1978</date>
                    </dateline>
                    <salute>To Fritz, Cy, Harold, Ham, Frank </salute>
                </opener>
                <p>The most important effort to be made during the next few days is to insure the
                    passage of the Panama Treaty.</p>
                <p>Work <hi rendition="#italic">hard</hi> on this &amp; coordinate your efforts.
                    Fritz will lead.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#bold">J.C.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d162-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d162-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Carter Library, Papers of Walter F. Mondale, Box 206, Middle East/Panama
                    (1/1/1978–1/20/1981). No classification marking. Sent to Mondale, Vance, Brown,
                    Jordan, and Moore.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
